{%- comment -%}
  Persist an idempotent result so a later retry with the same key replays it
  (spec §16.3). For mutating tools the caller invokes this INSIDE the business
  transaction, so the mutation and this record commit or roll back together — a
  mutation can never commit without its replay record, and a rolled-back call
  leaves no record (so a retry legitimately re-executes).

  @param {string}  key
  @param {string}  principal_id
  @param {string}  tool_name
  @param {string}  input_sha256   - guards against key reuse with different args
  @param {string}  response_json  - the cached MCP result, already JSON-serialized
  @param {integer} window         - seconds until the entry expires
{%- endcomment -%}
{% liquid
  assign now_unix = 'now' | to_time | strftime: '%s' | plus: 0
  assign exp = now_unix | plus: window
  graphql _ = 'modules/mcp/idempotency/create', key: key, principal_id: principal_id, tool_name: tool_name, input_sha256: input_sha256, response_json: response_json, expires_at: exp
  return true
%}
